;; A #row{...} (kind [*]) cannot be the type of a *value* -- only a type
;; argument to a row-kinded ('^&') constructor parameter. This used to be
;; silently accepted (and dropped the row's elements); now it is a kind error.
;; See docs/archive/history/row-type-in-value-position-loses-elements.md.
(defn f [x : #row{int bool}] : int 5)
